{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/530657-what-s-happening-to-my-body-random-embraces","id":530657,"title":"What's Happening To My Body? [Random Embraces!]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-27T22:01:37-07:00","id":530657,"title":"What's Happening To My Body? [Random Embraces!]","content":"So, I decided to whip this up; you take a mortal and toss 6 d10s. Go through the tables in order.<br /> <br /> <b>[1] Clan</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Daeva (+1 Dexterity)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Daeva (+1 Manipulation)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Gangrel (+1 Composure)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Gangrel (+1 Stamina)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Mekhet (+1 Intelligence)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Mekhet (+1 Wits)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Nosferatu (+1 Composure)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Nosferatu (+1 Strength)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Ventrue (+1 Presence)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Ventrue (+1 Resolve)</td> </tr> </table></div> <b>[2] Covenant</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">1-2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Carthians</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">3-4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Circle of the Crone (If a 0 is rolled on [3], final Discipline dot is Cruac. Check 4th die against [4a] instead of [4])</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">5-6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Invictus</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">7-8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Lancea et Sanctum (If a 0 is rolled on [3], final Discipline dot is Theban Sorcery. Check 4th die against [4b] instead of [4])</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">9-0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Ordo Dracul (If a 0 is rolled on [3], final Discipline dot is a dot in their Primary Coil. Check 4th die against [4c] instead of [4])</td> </tr> </table></div> <b>[3] Clan Disciplines</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">2 dots of A</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">2-3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">1 dot of A, 1 dot of B</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">2 dots of B</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">5-6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">1 dot of B, 1 dot of C</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">2 dots of C</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">8-9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">1 dot of A, 1 dot of C</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Reroll</td> </tr> </table></div> A is the first Discipline in the alphabetical listing of a Clan's Disciplines, B is the second, and C is the third.<br /> <br /> <b>[4] Final Discipline Dot</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Animalism</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\"><i>Auspex</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Celerity</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\"><i>Dominate</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\"><i>Majesty</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\"><i>Nightmare</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Obfuscate</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\"><i>Protean</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Resilience</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Vigor</td> </tr> </table></div> <b>[4a] Starting Rite (Cruac)</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">1-2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Pangs of Proserpina</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">3-4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Rigor Mortis</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">5-6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Mantle of Amorous Flames</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">7-8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">The Pool of Forbidden Truths</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">9-0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Reroll</td> </tr> </table></div> <b>[4b] Starting Miracles (Theban)</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Blood Scourge</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Blood Scourge [Even], Vitae Reliquary [Odd]</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Vitae Reliquary</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Blandishment of Sin</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Blandishment of Sin [Even], Apple of Sin [Odd]</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Apple of Eden</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Marian Apparition</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Marian Apparition [Even], Revelatory Shroud [Odd]</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Revelatory Shroud</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Reroll</td> </tr> </table></div> <b>[4c] Mystery Coil (Mysteries of the Dragon)</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">1-2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Mystery of the Ascendent</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">3-4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Mystery of the Wyrm</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">5-6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Mystery of the Voivode</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">7-8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Mystery of Zirnitra</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">9-10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 1px\">Mystery of \u017diva</td> </tr> </table></div> <b>[5 &amp; 6] Mask and Dirge Archetype</b><br /> Roll for Mask first, then Dirge. The numbers next to the archetypes reference the result rolled on die #2 when rolling for the Mask, and those rolled on die #3 when rolling for Dirge. If you previously rolled a number next to multiple archetypes in the same row, you may choose which is used. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Authoritarian {1,4,7,0}, Idealist {2,5,8,0}, Questioner {3,6,9,0}</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Child {1,4,7,0}, Jester {2,5,8,0}, Social Chameleon {3,6,9,0}</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Competitor {1,4,7,0}, Junkie {2,5,8,0}, Sadist {3,6,9,0}</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Conformist {1,4,7,0}, Martyr {2,5,8,0}, Scholar {3,6,9,0}</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Conspirator {1,4,7,0}, Masochist {2,5,8,0}, Rebel {3,6,9,0}</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Courtesan {1,4,7,0}, Monster {2,5,8,0}, Spy {3,6,9,0}</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Cult Leader {1,4,7,0}, Nomad {2,5,8,0}, Survivor {3,6,9,0}</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Deviant {1,4,7,0}, Nurturer {2,5,8,0}, Teacher {3,6,9,0}</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Follower {1,4,7,0}, Perfectionist {2,5,8,0}, Visionary {3,6,9,0}</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 5px\">Guru {Odd}, Penitent {Even}</td> </tr> </table></div> <hr /><br /> 6d10, in order, gets <i>me</i>...<br /> <br /> 1: A dextrous Daeva...<br /> 2: ... who's a Carthian, no less!<br /> 9: His starting Discipline dots are Celerity, Vigor...<br /> 5: ... and Majesty! Stereotypical Daeva is Stereotypical<br /> 6: His Mask is that he's a Monster, but his <i>true</i> self, his Dirge, is...<br /> 6: A Spy? A Spy!<br /> <br /> I could figure out something from that. Still, let's try again and see if we can get something more interesting.<br /> <br /> 6: A Mekhet with her Wits around her...<br /> 1: ... who's also a Carthian. Just like Unsubtle McGee up there.<br /> 7: Two dots of Obfuscate? Stealthy Mekhet is Stealthy<br /> 0: And she gets a dot of Vigor, perfect for those SNEAK ATTACKS!<br /> 0: To the outside world, she's a Guru, a source of wisdom and advice, but privately...<br /> 9: She just wants to follow someone else. She obviously joined the Carthian Movement because all the cool kids were doing it.<br /> <br /> This is actually really damn fun:<br /> <br /> 9: A Ventrue with some Presence about them. I can dig it.<br /> 8: A priestly Vampire at that/<br /> 6: A dot of Dominate, a dot of Resilience...<br /> 4 : ...make that <i>two</i> dots of Dominate.<br /> 0: Outwardly, they make a show of being penitent, but inwardly...<br /> 5: ...it's all just part of some grand conspiracy!<br /> <br /> Anyone else want to hop onto <a href=\"http://anydice.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Anydice</a> and give it a shot? Extra points if you can come up with something internally consistent! I'll probably up it to 7 dice tomorrow, so you can generate your Touchstone randomly as well. You know, so you can autopilot character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 05-28-2015, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T06:18:38-07:00","id":530919,"title":"","content":"This seems like a fun way to make NPCs! Let me try;<br /> <br /> 0,8,8,5,2,6.<br /> <br /> Alright, so;<br /> Nobody takes Father Briaries seriously. When they look at him, all they see is a Jester, a twit capable of some Animalism and Resilience, but nothing of true note. No one's figured out yet his slow development of the arts of Majesty. And why should he let them? If they look too deep, they might begin to wonder. For example, they might think to ask why the Sanctified was seen with a number of Kindred who would soon be slain by &quot;VII&quot;. Because, in truth, the Father is a monster's Monster. He enjoys the look on the faces of his fellow Vampires as he takes their life far too much to ever stop. So he plays the fool, and bides his time....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T16:45:17-07:00","id":532545,"title":"","content":"3, 1, 9, 8, 4, 1<br /> <br /> Kay Faulkner is not the Movement's greatest heroine. Though she's a Gangrel, running wild with the Beast, she keeps it tightly under wraps most of the time; involved in various interest groups in the city, she parrots party lines and popular literature without thinking, and her arguments seem to be quoted. She doesn't have the originality, she doesn't have the rage and (since she seems only to use her insectile Beast to stay out of trouble and evade the authorities, shapeshifting to escape trouble and asking animals to stand watch) she doesn't seem to have the courage to change <i>anything</i>. In reality, though, Kay has quietly been working out unified theories about the failings of political movements, preparing a dossier on how the Movement could best optimize its approach; when she finally pipes up in her quiet, level voice, buzzing and thin, she may bring the current Carthian leadership to its knees.<br /> 8, 7, 1, 2, 6, 5<br /> Lieselotte is one of the Second Estate's dark nuns, a tall, muscular woman with decayed eyes and writhing black wounds at her brow. A devoted Mason in life, in death, she considers herself the mistress of a crew of seducer priests and priestesses, mostly Daeva (whose state she constantly checks up on with Auspex), serving the Lance's interests in taking control of the city - as well as in seeking ancient religious artifacts and control over mortal society. In public, she puts on a show of being Mother Damnable, paying lip service to the Lancea et Sanctum and looking the other way when those around her, Kindred and kine, want to slake their thirsts... and carefully noting down who needs to relive their pleasures in Nightmares, with Lieselotte, a writhing, judgmental worm-Marian, taking the place of their gorgeous partner.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T17:29:24-07:00","id":532597,"title":"","content":"I honestly didn't expect people to like this that much. I might have to do more of these.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T17:45:49-07:00","id":532608,"title":"","content":"7 - 1 - 3 - 1 - 9 - 1 - 2 - 9<br /> Ernesto Romero was a quiet child, which creeped everyone out. He would follow the cliques of his peers in high school and college, but was always the quiet guy. People who noticed him often questioned why he was there, but he would just shrug and give a lingering stare that would cause others to back away. His only real friend was his rat, Willardo. A local Nos observed him for a month, seeing potential in Ernesto to be a spy. The little man was Embraced, and now pretty much does the same thing he did when he was living, only now, with a\u2026 different\u2026 clique.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1840-akashicmonk","name":"akashicmonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1840_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T08:29:08-07:00","id":534337,"title":"","content":"I had to go check the rulebook. I had never played with the rule that the third dot can come from anywhere! I must have just glazed over the text that said it was possible. Now I'm rolling up characters and can't stop giggling at Daeva's with Protean, Nosferatu with Auspex, and Venture with Nightmare. It just seems taboo. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T08:35:31-07:00","id":534373,"title":"","content":"And now a Mekhet with nightmare! :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}